<?xml version='1.0' encoding='UTF-8'?>
<!--
     this file contains a list of all modules needed for your application
     on a specific machine. It commonly starts with the own project and
     modules.

     note that the comm-objects directories should *not* be listed here.
     The module name you list here must be one of the folders in the given
     project.

     Each listed external project must start with a <url> tag that defines
     the path to a git repository. If you have environment variables (like
     DAPPS_GITROOT_base=....) , you can use the prefix dgrbase: (etc) to get
     a shorter url.

     The URL for the own or main project is not needed. Instead, this
     project has the attribute main="true".

     If you encounter a message that a certain comm-objects folder cannot
     be found, use dueca-gproject borrow-project to add that project url.
     Alternatively, you can add a <project>..</project> tag here with the
     project url tag in it.

     If you need to check out from a specific branch, version or
     revision, add a <version>...</version> tag to specify branch, tag or
     the git hash.
-->
<machine xmlns="https://dueca.tudelft.nl/modules"
  xmlns:xsi="http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema-instance"
  xsi:schemaLocation="https://dueca.tudelft.nl/modules https://dueca.tudelft.nl/schemas/modules.xsd">
  <project main="true">
  </project>
</machine>